reagent-name-rmcgenerictoxin = Generic Toxin
reagent-desc-rmcgenerictoxin = General identification for many similar toxins, sometimes created as a byproduct through chemical reactions.

reagent-name-rmcmolecularacid = Diluted Molecular Acid
reagent-desc-rmcmolecularacid = An acid of unknown composition, this sample doesn't seem to be as dangerous those found within Xenonid bloodstreams.

rmc-body-stings = Your body stings slightly.

reagent-name-rmclexorin = Lexorin
reagent-desc-rmclexorin = Lexorin is an extremely dangerous compound that damages tissue and paralyzes the lungs, effectively stopping respiration. Can be deadly in even small doses. Lexorin is effectively countered by variants of dexalin.

reagent-name-rmcmindbreakertoxin = Mindbreaker Toxin
reagent-desc-rmcmindbreakertoxin = A powerful hallucinogenic compound that is illegal under Marine Law. Causes extreme hallucinations and is very addictive. Formerly known as LSD.

reagent-name-rmcblackgoo = Black Goo
reagent-desc-rmcblackgoo = A strange substance of unknown origin. . .

reagent-name-rmc-chloral-hydrate = Chloral Hydrate
reagent-desc-rmc-chloral-hydrate = Chloral hydrate was the first synthetically produced sedative-hypnotic drug. It is a powerful sedative which causes near instant sleepiness, but can be deadly in large quantities. Often used together with other anesthetics for surgical procedures.

reagent-name-rmcunstablemutagen = Unstable Mutagen
reagent-desc-rmcunstablemutagen = A mutagenic compound used in experimental botany. Can cause unpredictable mutations in plants, but is very lethal to humans.

reagent-name-rmcdinitroaniline = Dinitroaniline
reagent-desc-rmcdinitroaniline = A class of chemical compounds used industrially in the production of pesticides and herbicides.

reagent-name-rmcpotassiumchloride = Potassium Chloride
reagent-desc-rmcpotassiumchloride = A bitter tasting salt that can be used as a spice, but can cause cardiac arrest in larger quantities. Has been used as a component in lethal injections for many years.

reagent-name-rmcpotassiumchlorophoride = Potassium Chlorophoride
reagent-desc-rmcpotassiumchlorophoride = A specific chemical based on Potassium Chloride used to stop the heart for surgery. Causes instant cardiac arrest. Not safe to eat!

reagent-name-rmcpotassiumphorosulfate = Potassium Phorosulfate
reagent-desc-rmcpotassiumphorosulfate = A chemical made from a violent reaction using sulphuric acid. Has specific industrial uses in sterilizing surfaces from biological contamination in non-human-accessible areas.

reagent-name-rmcironsulfate = Iron Sulfate
reagent-desc-rmcironsulfate = A reactive sulfide material often used as an intermediate or starting component in various chemical processes.

reagent-name-rmcironphoridesulfate = Iron Phoride Sulfate
reagent-desc-rmcironphoridesulfate = Iron Sulfate combined with Phoron to form a robust and durable substance, usually proposed as an additive to armor plates. Saw little actual use due to its flammability.

reagent-name-rmccoppersulfate = Copper Sulfate
reagent-desc-rmccoppersulfate = A common fungicide that is widely used to treat wood and other organic materials to prevent rot, decay, and fungal growth.

reagent-name-rmcformaldehyde = Formaldehyde
reagent-desc-rmcformaldehyde = A toxic organic gas mostly used in making resins, polymers, and explosives. Known to be a natural carcinogen.

reagent-name-rmcparaformaldehyde = Paraformaldehyde
reagent-desc-rmcparaformaldehyde = A polymerized form of formaldehyde, slowly formed in a cold aqueous solution.

reagent-name-rmcamatoxin = Amatoxin
reagent-desc-rmcamatoxin = A powerful poison derived from certain species of mushroom.

reagent-name-rmcphenolformaldehyderesin = Phenol-Formaldehyde Resin
reagent-desc-rmcphenolformaldehyderesin = A common molding polymer used in the production of many small parts. Has great stress capacity and has proven itself over many decades.

reagent-name-rmcpolytrinicacid = Polytrinic Acid
reagent-desc-rmcpolytrinicacid = An extremely corrosive acid capable of dissolving a broad range of materials very quickly.

reagent-name-rmcsoporific = Soporific
reagent-desc-rmcsoporific = An effective hypnotic used to treat insomnia. Concentrated soporific is used as a surgical anesthetic.
